id: pm-web-4p94
title: Default catalog freshness tests interpret a partial sibling worktree farm as the complete fleet
description: "Catalog tests default the fleet root to the package parent. In a worktree farm containing only some package worktrees, the tests infer an incomplete expected catalog and reject the complete committed snapshot. Reproduced while refreshing pm-web-5hdb: 22/24 focused tests passed with implicit discovery; selecting the canonical fleet through PM_FLEET_ROOT passed 24/24. Distinct from the corrected identity/deduplication behavior in pm-web-cqwm. Improve default root selection or distinguish partial discovery without weakening standalone snapshot checks. No hosted scope."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[2]: catalog,testing
created_at: "2026-10-15T23:07:53.640Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T11:01:31.050Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T11:26:38.059Z",codex-agent,"Related fleet-root workaround caveat reproduced during pm-web-pep7: a relative PM_FLEET_ROOT reaches scripts/read-fleet-commands.ts without normalization, so the dependency symlink created inside a disposable package copy points relative to that copy instead of the source checkout. The optional command-snapshot test then reports a missing @typesafe-ai/sdk dependency for Jev despite the canonical checkout dependency being present. Resolving the same fleet root at invocation time made the complete command-snapshot check pass. Follow-up: normalize the configured fleet root before constructing disposable dependency symlinks, alongside the existing partial-sibling root-selection work. No implementation or threshold changes for this follow-up."
  "2026-10-17T11:01:31.050Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 release attempts provide a controlled topology comparison: the package worktree fails catalog membership and live-fleet snapshot equality, while an isolated standalone copy passes those same checks. All 258 TypeScript/CSS source files were verified byte-identical between the two copies, and both use fresh HOME with global/system Git config disabled. The standalone profile matches CI and uses independent test storage. No catalog source, fixture roster, snapshot or test condition changed."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  scripts/read-fleet-commands.ts,project
  test/fleet-commands.test.ts,project
body: ""
